Brown puddings are actually easier.  They split when hit with a metal
object, just like black, but they rot cloth and leather, as opposed to 
corroding metal, and they aren't as tough.  The drawback is they have
less hitpoints to begin with so it takes a lot longer to build up the
farm. 

There is no way to increase the hitpoints of non-drinking monsters,
except to kill them and turn undead (they can come back with more, but
there is still a max).

I have a system where I divide and heal the ones with 69 hps, and kill
off the others.  

I also name them every now and then, by the turn number usually, so that
I can track their lifecycle and flow.  

This is boring, tedious and dangerous, yes, but in comparison to all the
other aspects of a long game (e.g., extinctionist), it's just another
thing.

